        "<p>A simplified representation of the surface boundary conditions is obtained by modeling the outermost layers of the star under the classical gray atmosphere approximation, where the optical depth is parameterized to match the transition from an optically thick interior to an optically thin space. Under the Eddington approximation, this matching is formulated at the photosphere, where the optical depth is exactly two-thirds, yielding a relation between the gas pressure, local gravity, and opacity:</p>"
